      "recent": [
        "You harvest late knotflax stand: 1 x KnotflaxSeedHeads.",
        "ÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍ",
        "Interact — choose a direction, or . for underfoot.",
        "ÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍÍ",
        "Interact — choose a direction, or . for underfoot.",
        "You see a public catch-cloth frame.\nIt shades the ground under it and the cells around it from the glare, for whoever stands there.\nFair weather; the edge collects during mild showers. Shared catchment: 3/3 water available this interval. The frames share one allowance; missed rain is not stored. The dry mesh can save chaff from a knotflax bundle.\nHow to use: Stand under it: it shades its own cell and the cells within 1 of it. During mild showers, stand beside the frame, press C and choose catch rain, then the exact carried flask or waterskin. Bring a knotflax seed-head bundle to the frame and winnow one plantable seed.\nNeeds: a compatible carried water vessel with room, and the intact public collecting edge; one gathered bundle and the intact public frame.\nCost and limits: It only matters where the sun does: in the Beating at the Height of the day, bareheaded in the open you gain a stack of Parched every 10 turns, and under shade the count does not run. A hat or a roof does the same. Carried or taken up, it shades nothing. Both frames share three water per shower interval. This is optional water for existing uses; fair weather costs nothing. In fair weather on dry ground, the frame can save the chaff for a fire. Otherwise the chaff is discarded. Winnowing takes one action, in any season, and uses no rainwater.\nRight now you cannot: catch rain (There are no mild showers now. Ordinary water sources still work).\n\nWaxed cloth on a fixed public frame gathers a little clean rainwater. Both frames share the allotment's catchment. During mild showers, press C here and choose a carried flask or waterskin. Ordinary water sources remain useful in fair weather."
      ],
